-name: Clerk
-
-# The outside party, asked once, at the moment its opinion is worth having.
-#
-# The clerk reads this repository without its context and can stop nothing.
-# Two jobs where having no context is the qualification rather than a
-# limitation: snag walks the work and lists what is unsound or does not match
-# what was written about it, and handover reads it as a stranger who has just
-# cloned it and lists what would stop them.
-#
-# WHY ready_for_review, AND NOT EVERY PUSH
-#
-# This spends a metered vendor and produces prose somebody reads once. On every
-# push it would be both waste and noise: a pull request iterates - a check
-# fails, it is fixed, it fails again - and the agent that opened it is a poor
-# judge of when that has finished. It always thinks it has.
-#
-# So the signal comes from the operator instead. Pull requests open as drafts,
-# every check runs and goes green while the fussing happens, and marking it
-# ready is the deliberate act that says the work is done and an opinion is now
-# wanted. It fires once, before approval, which is the only point at which the
-# findings are still actionable.
-#
-# Re-requesting is a review request, which fires this again - so acting on the
-# findings and asking for a fresh read costs one click and one call.
-#
-# WHAT IT MAY NOT DO
-#
-# Nothing. It has no lever by construction: findings are SARIF at note level,
-# and the code scanning results check MUST STAY OUT of main's required checks.
-# A removal or a criticism that blocks a merge is the outside party acquiring
-# exactly the power this design withholds.
-
-on:
-  pull_request:
-    # Elevation only. Never opened, never synchronize - those are the states
-    # where the work is still moving.
-    #
-    # review_requested is deliberately NOT here, and was removed after being
-    # tried. It fires on ANY reviewer request, and CODEOWNERS requests one
-    # automatically the moment a pull request is elevated - so a single
-    # elevation fired this twice, and the concurrency group below cancelled one
-    # of them by luck rather than by design, part-way through a metered call.
-    # The clerk cannot be requested as a reviewer either, so there was nothing
-    # to filter on.
-    types: [ready_for_review]
-
-  # Asked again, without changing the pull request's state.
-  #
-  #   @clerk snag       walk the work again
-  #   @clerk handover   read it again as a stranger
-  #
-  # The Dependabot shape, and it beats re-requesting a review: it is explicit,
-  # it works on a draft, it says which reading is wanted, and it leaves a record
-  # in the conversation of who asked for what.
